## MCP Architecture

### Server Discovery

MCP servers are configured in the project's `mcps/` directory:

```
mcps/
├── user-presc-source/          # Source Presc MCP server
│   ├── tools/                  # Tool definitions
│   └── resources/              # Resource definitions
├── user-presc-target/          # Target Presc MCP server
├── user-analyzax-self-hosted-supabase/  # Supabase integration
├── user-presc-target-adv/      # Advanced Target Presc
├── user-n8n-mcp-advanced-main/ # n8n workflow automation
├── user-n8n-mcp-default/       # n8n default
└── user-notebooks/             # Notebook integration
└── user-visualization/          # Visualization server
```

Each server folder contains:
- **`tools/`** — JSON descriptor files for each available tool
- **`resources/`** — JSON descriptor files for each available resource
- **`serverUseInstructions.md`** (optional) — Server-specific guidance

### Tool Descriptor Format

Tools are defined as JSON files in the server's `tools/` directory:

```json
{
  "name": "tool-name",
  "description": "What this tool does",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "param1": { "type": "string", "description": "Parameter 1" },
      "param2": { "type": "number", "description": "Parameter 2" }
    },
    "required": ["param1"]
  }
}
```

### Resource Descriptor Format

Resources are defined as JSON files in the server's `resources/` directory:

```json
{
  "uri": "mcp://server-name/resource-name",
  "name": "Resource Name",
  "description": "What this resource provides",
  "mimeType": "application/json"
}
```

