## Security Considerations

### Principle of Least Privilege

- Configure MCP servers with minimum required permissions
- Use service accounts with scoped access where possible
- Rotate credentials regularly
- Monitor MCP tool usage for anomalies

### Data Protection

- MCP tools may have access to sensitive data (databases, APIs, filesystems)
- Never expose MCP credentials in conversation history
- Validate tool inputs before passing to MCP servers
- Be aware of data exfiltration risks when connecting to external services

### Server Trust

- Only configure MCP servers from trusted sources
- Review server tool definitions before enabling
- Understand what each tool does and its permissions
- Audit MCP server configurations periodically

### Smart Mode Approval

When auto-review blocks an MCP call:
- `requestSmartModeApproval`: Set to `true` only after auto-review blocks
- `smartModeBlockReason`: Provide the exact block reason returned by auto-review
- The user must approve through the native approval card

