## Tool Selection Guidelines

| Scenario | Use | Why |
|---|---|---|
| File operations | Read, Write, StrReplace, Delete | Direct, fast, no external dependency |
| Search | Grep (ripgrep), Glob | Built-in, fast, optimized |
| External data access | MCP tools | Standardized interface to external systems |
| Web content | WebFetch, WebSearch | Purpose-built for HTTP fetches |
| Shell commands | Shell | Native terminal integration |
| Code analysis | SemanticSearch | Meaning-based, not exact-match |

**Rule**: Use built-in tools (Read, Write, Grep, Shell) for internal operations. Use MCP tools only when connecting to external systems that are not accessible through built-in tools.

